{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "The Environment", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Fish Farming", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 7, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 2, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe ways of solving problems and getting things done social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "  Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Passive: The Present Continuous and Present Perfect Tenses", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<p>You use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Continuous</span> to talk about an action that is happening at the time of speaking. The action or event is in progress. <br/><span class=\"italic\">Now that so many fish <span class=\"strong\">are becoming</span> extinct, the time has come to find an alternative.</span></p><p>You use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span> to talk about a finished action or event with present consequences. There is a connection between what happened in the past and the present.<br/><span class=\"italic\">The time <span class=\"strong\">has come</span> to find an alternative.</span></p>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You often choose the passive form when you want to talk about an action but are not so interested in saying who or what does/did it. Passives without <span class=\"italic\">agents</span> (the doers) are common in academic and scientific writing. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Look at the chart below for the structure of the passive voice.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Name\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Structure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">am</span>/<span class=\\\"italic\\\">are</span>/<span class=\\\"italic\\\">is</span> +  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">being </span>+ past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Species of fish <span class=\\\"strong\\\">are being wiped out</span>. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">have</span>/<span class=\\\"italic\\\">has</span> + <span class=\\\"italic\\\">been </span>+ past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">These <span class=\\\"strong\\\">have been dumped</span> directly into the coastal waters nearby and the biological life there is being endangered.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "For years now, we have been told by environmentalists about the dangers of overfishing in the world's oceans. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Species of fish are being wiped out. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Now that so many fish are becoming extinct, the time has come to find an alternative.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "They are also being fed ocean fish, such as anchovies and mackerel. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Simple Past Tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You use the <span class=\"strong\">Simple Past</span> tense to talk about many kinds of past events: short, quickly finished actions, longer situations and repeated events. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Usually, when you use the <span class=\"strong\">Simple Past</span> tense, the time of the finished action is clear from the context or explicitly mentioned in the sentence.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">For a long time, people <span class=\"strong\">thought</span> it was the solution to the problem of overfishing.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Here is another example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">\u201cFish farming is not the answer to feeding the world's population,\u201d <span class=\"strong\">said</span> a well-known environmentalist. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Remember that there are both regular and irregular verbs. Look at the chart for examples of the <span class=\"strong\">Simple Past</span> tense verbs.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Regular Verb</div>\\\"}\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Irregular Verb</div>\\\"}\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Present </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Past</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Present </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Past</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"discover\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"discovered\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"think\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"thought\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"recognize\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"recognized\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"say\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"said\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "For a long time, people thought it was the solution to the problem of overfishing.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "\u201cFish farming is not the answer to feeding the world's population,\u201d said a well-known environmentalist. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "environmentalist", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person who is interested in learning about and protecting the environment", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We have been told by environmentalists about the dangers of overfishing.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le02ob07aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about the consequences of fish farming", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "overfishing ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "making the number of fish too low by taking too many fish from waterways", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Overfishing threatens marine life.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le02ob07aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "multi-million dollar", "type": "name"}, {"content": "costing millions of dollars", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Fish farming is a multi-million dollar industry.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le02ob07aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "one-third ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "one of three equal parts", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Fish farming produces one third of the fish eaten in the world today.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le02ob07aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "anchovy ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " a very small fish that tastes strongly of salt", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Anchovies and mackerel feed  some ocean fish.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le02ob07aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "waste ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "unwanted materials or substances that are left after you have used something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Fish farms create animal waste and dangerous chemicals.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le02ob07aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "prohibited ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "not allowed", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Fish farming should be prohibited.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le02ob07aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Visit your local fish store and find out where the fish is caught or farmed.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Talk to the fisherman/salesperson about the fish. Find out as much information as you can.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write notes in English about what you discovered.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share and discuss the information with a partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I visit my local fishmonger.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk to them about the fish and where it is from.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I gather as much information as I can.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share and discuss the information with a partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"content": "engenn9le02ob07re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "template_override": 1, "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can describe social and urban change, and environmental problems.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about things that happened.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about thi